{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pulls/11107","id":5482993545,"node_id":"PR_kwDOV4BIxs8AAAABRs_XiQ","html_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/11107","diff_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/11107.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/11107.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/11107","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pulls/11107/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pulls/11107/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/issues/11107/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/statuses/61604cf11044939de7e24293b9b88c7f5b5e561c","number":11107,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"L-meta-5228: exclude two nested dirty ANDs under the G11 gate budget","user":{"login":"HaoranLiao","id":16676497,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2Njc2NDk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16676497?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HaoranLiao","html_url":"https://github.com/HaoranLiao","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HaoranLiao/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HaoranLiao/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HaoranLiao/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HaoranLiao/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HaoranLiao/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HaoranLiao/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HaoranLiao/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HaoranLiao/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HaoranLiao/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This proves L-meta-5228 for the specified 11-vertex graph. Under the registered hypotheses, a least top-form fan-in-two AND/OR circuit with two nested dirty AND gates cannot have at most 21 gates and three unowned edges while satisfying the residual-cover and gate-count bounds.\n\nFor a residual cover of size four, the three unowned edges form an induced matching. Restricting the circuit to the six endpoints gives three positive edge inputs and eight independent inputs. At a top AND that accepts an edge, the witness supplies one dirty AND. The opposite operand supplies a true input pin or the other dirty AND. The proof checks that these possibilities cannot account for all three edges.\n\nFor larger minimum covers, the gate count and the single-OR cases leave five stars and two mixing OR gates. The proof traces their dirty signals and the raw input common to each mixer’s receiving operands. Of the 560 ways to choose three edges, 204 admit candidate covers for this check, giving 465 choices of an edge triple and a cover. The kernel verifies the certificates for the star centres, leaves and common inputs against independent inputs of the graph.\n\nThe cone recursion and transitivity, OR-path characterization, and wire evaluation equations build on willakone’s earlier proofs. [PR 3111](https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/3111) · [PR 3118](https://github.com/open-goat/pequalnp-proofs/pull/3118)\n\nThe project checker returned `ACCEPTED (check)` against the published statement. It rechecked 3,249 constants and reported only `propext`, `Quot.sound` and `Classical.choice`.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-25T00:53:39Z","updated_at":"2026-11-25T00:53:39Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"7d6a3063d8e6ac9fe64b2cd0526ed29cbd90e54b","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"HaoranLiao:L-meta-5228","ref":"L-met